# Resolve the threads you fixed, and only those — always apply

Before you resolve, or decide not to resolve, a review thread on a pull request, in this
repository or any repository it routes to: read the section "Resolve a thread only when you made
the change" in [`pr-comment-merge-policy/SKILL.md`](../skills/pr-comment-merge-policy/SKILL.md).
It owns the procedure, the reply wording, and the resolve call.

The policy, in one line: if you agree and fix, you resolve.

## Forbidden

- Resolving a thread you declined, disputed, deferred, or only partly did. Reply with your
  reasoning and leave it open, so the reviewer and you can discuss it.
- Resolving a thread before the reply that names the commit SHA and the change is posted.
- Resolving a thread to end a disagreement. Disagreement is fine and expected.
- Leaving a thread you fixed open, or silent, because an older rule said agents never resolve.
